Hi Juan,

If you only want to plot Greek letters or equations into ggplot labels or annotations I strongly suggest you use the expression() statement.

There are numerous examples online on how to use the syntax.

I suspect that the package you are using is not maintained for the latest versions of R and ggplot and I don't see the reason to downgrade really.
Here's sth to get you started.

https://stackoverflow.com/questions/5293715/how-to-use-greek-symbols-in-ggplot2

Then remember ^is superscript [] is subscript and you replace the regular space with the ~ in the syntax.

Just a few random tips. If you have a specific problem on syntax don't hesitate to ask!

Good luck end enjoy ggplot!
